Binary Search:
Binary Search repeatedly divides the search range into two halves and eliminates the half where the element cannot exist.

Case	        Time Complexity
Best Case        	O(1)
Average Case	    O(log n)
Worst Case	       O(log n)
Space Complexity	 O(1) 

The array must be sorted before applying Binary Search.
Best case occurs when the target is exactly at the middle.
Each comparison eliminates approximately half of the remaining elements.
It is much faster than Linear Search for large sorted datasets.
